  {
   "key": "federal-senate-2144",
   "date": "2011-11-07",
   "house": "senate",
   "question": "This division relates to the Policy _[For a carbon price](/policies/3)_. The majority voted against an [amendment](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2011-11-07.313.1) that progress be reported,(See [[http://www.aph.gov.au/About\\_Parliament/Senate/Powers\\_practice\\_n\\_procedures/](http://www.aph.gov.au/About_Parliament/Senate/Powers_practice_n_procedures/)~/link.aspx?\\_id=DE8C9D42F0B74C93A8AA5C680A617E0C&\\_z=z here] for more information about these procedural motions. ) moved by Liberal Senator [Cory Bernardi](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Cory_Bernardi&mpc=Senate&house=senate). Senator Bernardi intended to subsequently seek leave to meet at a later hour so they could continue to debate the bills. He did this in order to extend the amount of time spent discussing the bills.(Read Senator Bernardi's reasoning for his motions [here](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2011-11-07.313.1).) The bills being debated were a package of eighteen bills to implement a carbon pricing mechanism, which is a key policy of the Australian Labor Party while in Government. The eighteen bills were: - [Clean Energy Bill 2011](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r4653) - [Clean Energy (Consequential Amendments) Bill 2011](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:legislation%2Fbillhome%2Fr4655) - [Clean Energy (Income Tax Rates Amendments) Bill 2011](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Fbillhome%2Fr4647%22) - [Clean Energy (Household Assistance Amendments) Bill 2011](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:legislation%2Fbillhome%2Fr4662) - [Clean Energy (Tax Laws Amendments) Bill 2011](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Fbillhome%2Fr4649%22) - [Clean Energy (Fuel Tax Legislation Amendment) Bill 2011](http://parlinfo.a",
   "stage": "In committee",
